    {
      "id": "poc-sortech",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2950,
      "y": 3640,
      "width": 1450,
      "height": 520,
      "text": "# Sortech\n## [[03_Projects/_Registry/PPJ_DISCOVERY_REGISTER|Sortech]]\n## Technology / SI Assessment\n### VENDOR EVALUATION (discovery item, not a project)\n\nScope: Potentially relevant to invoice automation, GRN workflows, WFX automation, reconciliation, approvals, agentic workflows and smart-factory integration.\nNo operational integration assumed.",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "poc-quanskill",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -4500,
      "y": 4210,
      "width": 1450,
      "height": 520,
      "text": "# Quanskill\n## [[03_Projects/_Registry/PPJ_DISCOVERY_REGISTER|Quanskill]]\n## Vendor / Product Evaluation\n### VENDOR EVALUATION (discovery item, not a project)\n\nScope: Not yet an approved implementation project.\nNo operational integration assumed.",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "hdr-grp-legend",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -4570,
      "y": 5000,
      "width": 274,
      "height": 130,
      "text": "# 09 LEGEND"
    },
    {
      "id": "legend-nodes",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -4500,
      "y": 5150,
      "width": 3000,
      "height": 780,
      "text": "# NODE CATEGORIES\n### WFX ERP - purple\n### Third-Party System - brown\n### GTAS Internal System - indigo\n### Data / Knowledge Platform - teal\n### Shared AI Platform - pink group\n### Project card colour = STATUS (below)\n\nThe class is on each card under the status: AI APPLICATION | AUTOMATION | WORKFLOW | DATA PLATFORM | INTERNAL PLATFORM | IOT | POC / EVALUATION | COLLABORATION | ARCHIVED"
    },
    {
      "id": "legend-edges",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -4500,
      "y": 5970,
      "width": 3000,
      "height": 780,
      "text": "# LINES\n### INTEGRATION - confirmed operational integration (green)\n### PLANNED - in scope or in development (orange)\n### DATA - data / knowledge dependency (blue)\n### AFFINITY - same business capability, no integration confirmed (grey)\n\nThe label always names the category; colour is never the only signal. Each project draws at most one AFFINITY line; its other related systems are listed on the card."
    },
    {
      "id": "legend-status",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -4500,
      "y": 6790,
      "width": 3000,
      "height": 780,
      "text": "# STATUS COLOUR\n### Green - Production / Operational\n### Blue - Active / Development\n### Yellow - UAT / Evaluation / Analysis\n### Orange - On Hold\n### Grey-blue - Maintenance / Support\n### Grey - Closed / Archived\n\nThe exact source status is written on each card under the project code."
    },
    {
      "id": "hdr-grp-collab",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10830,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 550,
      "height": 130,
      "text": "# 07 EXTERNAL COLLABORATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "proj-ext-academiccollaboration-v1-1-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10900,
      "y": 170,
      "width": 1450,
      "height": 520,
      "text": "# Academic Collaboration (UIT)\n## [[03_Projects/PPJ.UIT.ACADEMIC.COLLABORATION.v1.1|EXT_AcademicCollaboration_v1.1.0]]\n## Active / Problem Framing\n### COLLABORATION\n\nDomain: External Collaboration\nBaseline code: PPJ.UIT.ACADEMIC.COLLABORATION.v1.1\nCapability: Academic collaboration: prototypes, research, competitions, talent pipeline. Not a production application.\nStream: EXTERNAL DEVELOPMENT.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "hdr-grp-arch",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10830,
      "y": 960,
      "width": 653,
      "height": 130,
      "text": "# 08 ARCHIVED / CLOSED ENABLEMENT"
    },
    {
      "id": "proj-ai-automation-workshop-202606",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10900,
      "y": 1110,
      "width": 1450,
      "height": 520,
      "text": "# AI Automation Workshop (June 2026)\n## [[03_Projects/AI Automation Workshop|AI.Automation.Workshop.202606]]\n## Closed\n### ARCHIVED (enablement)\n\nDomain: External Collaboration\nCapability: Workshop record. No active tasks.",
      "color": "#8c8c8c"
    },
    {
      "id": "proj-ai-automation-workshop-analysis-202606",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10900,
      "y": 1680,
      "width": 1450,
      "height": 520,
      "text": "# Workshop Analysis (June 2026)\n## [[03_Projects/Workshop Analysis|AI.Automation.Workshop.Analysis.202606]]\n## Closed\n### ARCHIVED (enablement)\n\nDomain: External Collaboration\nCapability: Workshop analysis record. No active tasks.\nNot in the 35-item baseline; present in the vault registry.",
      "color": "#8c8c8c"
    },
    {
      "id": "proj-vitas-sharing-202606",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10900,
      "y": 2250,
      "width": 1450,
      "height": 520,
      "text": "# VITAS Sharing (June 2026)\n## [[03_Projects/VITAS Sharing|VITAS.Sharing.202606]]\n## Closed\n### ARCHIVED (external engagement)\n\nDomain: External Collaboration\nCapability: External sharing record. No active tasks.",
      "color": "#8c8c8c"
    },
    {
      "id": "guide",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10800,
      "y": 3020,
      "width": 3200,
      "height": 1300,
      "text": "# HOW TO READ THIS CANVAS\n\n### Centre, top to bottom: shared AI platforms, GTAS, third-party, WFX ERP core, data / knowledge foundation.\n### Left and right: AI & Automation projects by business domain.\n### Position is not architecture. A line exists only where a vault document supports it.\n\nIt is a layered ecosystem, not a strict dependency stack. The line label says how strong the relationship is; no line means no relationship is documented. Most links are AFFINITY - nothing is drawn as INTEGRATION unless a validated flow exists."
    },
    {
      "id": "hdr-grp-gap",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10830,
      "y": 4540,
      "width": 498,
      "height": 130,
      "text": "# DATA / GOVERNANCE GAPS"
    },
    {
      "id": "gap-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10900,
      "y": 4690,
      "width": 3000,
      "height": 640,
      "text": "## GAP 1 - Expense invoices merged\n\nThe 35-item baseline lists PPJ.ExpenseInvoices.v1.1 and LOG.EXPENSE.INVOICES.V1.2 as two projects. The vault registry (PPJ_PORTFOLIO_SNAPSHOT_20260918) already maps both to ONE project, LOG_ExpenseInvoiceProcessing_v1.2.2, and lists a decision still open: confirm the mapping and whether the earlier Export exclusion applies.\n\nDrawn as one node (vault registry outranks the baseline). Both baseline names are kept on the card.\n\nVault also holds two closed records outside the baseline: EXIM.ExpenseInvoices.Automation.v1.1 and AI.Automation.Workshop.Analysis.202606 - hence 36 records at the time of writing."
    },
    {
      "id": "gap-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10900,
      "y": 5370,
      "width": 3000,
      "height": 640,
      "text": "## GAP 2 - Canonical codes and status\n\nACC.GRNInvoiceMatching.v2.3 (baseline) vs ACC_GRNSupplierInvoiceBot_v2.3.0 (vault canonical). The vault says the GRNInvoiceMatching name is misleading; the canonical code is used.\n\nPPJxStratova.AI: baseline says Active PoC; vault says Closed and tracks the live PoC as DISCOVERY_PatternGenerationPoC. Vault used.\n\nPPJ.GLPI.Helpdesk.AI.Chatbot.v1.0: baseline says Merchandising / Shared; vault domain is Internal Chatbot & AI Platforms. Vault used."
    },
    {
      "id": "gap-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10900,
      "y": 6050,
      "width": 3000,
      "height": 640,
      "text": "## GAP 3 - Systems inventory\n\nSource: owner's operating-systems diagram. GTAS has 16 applications, not 15: GTAS Costing was missing from the list in circulation.\n\nMMSx (diagram) vs MMX (2026-09-18 ecosystem note): treated as one system, name unconfirmed.\n\nThe Finance AI canvas also names GTAS Factory, Quantity, Efficiency and ID. None is on the diagram; alias or separate application is unconfirmed.\n\nThe red star on GTAS Costing and the green highlight on Production Planning are shown but their meaning is not stated."
    },
    {
      "id": "gap-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10900,
      "y": 6730,
      "width": 3000,
      "height": 640,
      "text": "## GAP 4 - Relationship evidence\n\nNo document confirms an integration at WFX-module or GTAS-application level. Those links are AFFINITY.\n\nExceptions drawn stronger: PUR_MaterialAllocation validated flow into WFX (INTEGRATION, validated flow only); FIN_InvoiceDownloader to VNPT (INTEGRATION); PUR_GDIAutomation WFX API, ADMIN_ExpenseManagement E-office and MER_CostingAgenticPlatform GTAS/IED contract are in scope but not delivered (PLANNED).\n\nStatus counts: baseline buckets and the recomputed buckets differ (e.g. UAT and Analysis are one bucket here), so the two rows are not directly comparable."
    }
  ],
